# Compose preview screenshot rendering (common-conventions-preview-metadata). These PNGs
# are an intermediate: the `metadata` task copies them into metadata_data/photos/<module>,
# which is what is committed and what release.sh reads. Committing them too would store
# every listing image twice. Remove this ignore if you ever want
# `validate<Variant>ScreenshotTest` to act as UI regression testing.
**/src/screenshotTest*/reference/
# Supertonic 3's TTS bundle - 107 MiB of mostly-int8 .maml plus its codepoint table and ten voice
# styles. Rebuild byte for byte with `python scripts/ml/fetch_supertonic.py`, which pins the
# upstream revision and every ONNX SHA-256. Ignored for the same reason as the two above: it is
# the largest asset in the tree, it is derived rather than authored, and committing it would put
# it in history permanently.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: a fresh checkout builds a :speech APK with **no voices**, and the
# TTS engine then advertises no languages (SupertonicBundle.isPresent is false) rather than
# failing on the first utterance. Run the script before cutting a release.
speech/src/main/assets/supertonic/*.maml
speech/src/main/assets/supertonic/*.bin

